.                         
.                 
.                 * Control variables: gender, with reference being female [2];
>  pla0009_v2
.                 * Deviation from PAP: we state to use pla0009_h. However, thi
> s is not present in the pl dataset.
.                 * Therefore we use pla0009_v2.
.                 rename pla0009_v2 gender

.         
.                 * Control variables: age and age squared, 
.                 gen age = syear - ple0010_h
(1,547 missing values generated)

.                 gen age_sqrd = age^2
(1,547 missing values generated)

.                 
.                 * Control variables: income, already there; plc0013_h
.                 rename plc0013_h income

.                 
.                 * Control variables: type of emplyoment, reference being full
> -time employed [1]; plb0022_h
.                 rename plb0022_h employment

.                 
.                 * Control variables: marital status , reference being married
> ; pgfamstd; 
.                 * according to the pap, we merge the first two (married as re
> ference)
.                 * Deviation from the PAP: Same issue as with gender. pld0131_
> h not present.
.                 * Therefore we use pld0131_v1
.                 gen marital_status = .
(6,110 missing values generated)

.                 
.                 * Merge categories 1 and 2 into 1 ("Married")
.                 replace marital_status = 1 if inlist(pgfamstd, 1, 2)
(2,773 real changes made)

. 
.                 * Keep others as-is
.                 replace marital_status = pgfamstd if !inlist(pgfamstd, 1, 2)
(1,847 real changes made)

.                 
.                 * Label the new variable
.                 label define marital_lbl 1 "Verheiratet" 3 "Ledig" 4 "Geschie
> den" 5 "Verwitwed" 6 "Ehepartner Ausland" 7 "Eingetragene gleichgeschlechtlic
> he Partnerschaft"

.                 label values marital_status marital_lbl

.                 label variable marital_status "Marital status (1 = Married)"

.                 
.                 * Control variable: having obtained a university degree; base
> d on pgpbbil02
.                 gen higher_education = .
(6,110 missing values generated)

.                 replace higher_education = 1 if pgpbbil02 > 0
(2,670 real changes made)

.                 replace higher_education = 0 if pgpbbil02 <= 0 | missing(pgpb
> bil02)
(4,930 real changes made)

.                 
.                 label variable higher_education "Binary if individual obtaine
> d higher education"

.                 
.                 * collect the variables necessary for the analysis
.                 keep pid syear plh0004 plh0004_rev num_daughters num_children
>  sumkids gender age age_sqrd income employment pld0131_v1 marital_status pgpb
> bil02 higher_education

.                 
. 
.                 save "$DATA/h2_dataset.dta", replace // save preprocessed dat
> aset
file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/5%-sample/h2_dataset.dta saved

.         
. 
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS *
. 
.         * We only filter for plausible values (non negative)
.  
.         * only those with children; num_children > 0 
.         drop if num_children <= 0
(1,976 observations deleted)

.         
.         * drop if missing values; use gender as main indicator
.         drop if missing(gender)
(762 observations deleted)

.         drop if gender < 0 
(10 observations deleted)

.         
.         * drop negative values for wage
.         drop if income < 0
(1,573 observations deleted)

.         
.         * drop if negative values for emplyoment
.         drop if employment < 0 
(0 observations deleted)

.         
.         * drop if marital status negative
.         drop if marital_status < 0 
(2 observations deleted)

.         
.         * drop where only one observations, otherwise can't use fixed effects
.         bysort pid: gen n_obs = _N

.         gen singleton = n_obs == 1

.         tab singleton

  singleton |      Freq.     Percent        Cum.
------------+-----------------------------------
          0 |      1,144       64.02       64.02
          1 |        643       35.98      100.00
------------+-----------------------------------
      Total |      1,787      100.00

.         drop if singleton == 1 
(643 observations deleted)

.         
. 
. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES *
. 
. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         
.         * Description:
.         * Again, we assume that nature randomly assigns the gender of childre
> n and based on the subset
.         * of people who became parents (unobserved variables might drive the 
> decision to become a parent
.         * in the first place), we estimate the effect of one additional daugh
> ter on a policial preferences 
.         * elicited using a 11-point likert scale, which we reverse coded to m
> ake it more intuitive 
.         * (higher values indicating higher more left-leaning political prefer
> ences)
.         * Additionally, we include control variables and subject fixed effect
> s. Finally,
.         * we use cluster robust standard errors on the subject level.
.         
.         xtset pid syear

Panel variable: pid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2005 to 2019, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

. 
. 
.         xtreg plh0004_rev num_daughters i.num_children ib2.gender age age_sqr
> d income i.employment i.marital_status i.higher_education i.syear, fe cluster
> (pid)
note: 7.num_children omitted because of collinearity.
note: 1.gender omitted because of collinearity.

